// generative/ — density and sample generation: GANs, flows, VAEs, diffusion.
//
// Sits on nn and optim. Every model here is trained, so every model here needs
// an optimiser; the ones that score pixels run on Conv2dParameter.
//
// The components without a model prefix belong here for the same reason
// message_passing did in gnn/: diffusion_forward, score_network, langevin_sampler,
// energy_function, gaussian_reparameterization, elbo and gradient_penalty are
// each used by exactly the model they belong to -- two files apiece at most --
// and by nothing outside this package. DDPM needs a score and a forward
// diffusion schedule; EBM needs an energy and a sampler; VAE and IWAE share a
// reparameterisation and an ELBO; WGAN-GP needs the penalty. Naming them after
// the model that consumes them would have meant five packages of two files.
// rl/ is imported for `box_muller`-adjacent sampling in the GANs and the
// normalizing flows: those draw noise from the core RNG, and the flows'
// base distribution is a Gaussian. The dependency is declared here rather than
// discovered by the compiler because a pre-split scan of the root package could
// not see it -- at that point the referencing files were still in the root and
// rl/ had already left.
import {
  "riantr/snn_mbt/core",
  "riantr/snn_mbt/nn",
  "riantr/snn_mbt/activ",
  "riantr/snn_mbt/optim",
  "riantr/snn_mbt/rl",
}
